{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Please here, my lords.</b> Here now, you are lords to me, since you have passed by me. Another interpretation: Here now, you need to set your mind against these wicked men, so that they will not recognize you — and this is sound advice." "<b>Turn aside now.</b> Bend the road toward my house by a roundabout path, so they will not recognize that you are entering there; therefore it says ״Turn aside״ (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And lodge and wash your feet.</b> But is it the way of people to lodge first and afterward wash? And furthermore, did Abraham not say to them first, ״Wash your feet״? Rather, Lot said thus: If the men of Sodom come and see that they have already washed their feet, they will invent charges against me and say, ״Two or three days have already passed since they came to your house and you did not inform us!״ Therefore he said: Better that they tarry here with the dust on their feet, so they will look as though they have just now arrived; therefore he said, ״Lodge״ first and afterward ״wash.״" "<b>And they said, No.</b> But to Abraham they said, ״So shall you do.״ From this: one refuses the lesser but does not refuse the great (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>For in the square we shall lodge.</b> Here כִּי serves in the sense of אֶלָּא — for they said, ״We will not turn aside to your house, but in the city square we shall lodge.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:26.481610838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}